        <item>
            <title>1.5.1</title>
            <pubDate>Sun, 05 Jul 2026 20:02:19 +0900</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>33</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>1.5.1</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[<h3>Fixed</h3>
<ul>
<li><b>The preview pane no longer freezes when you open a folder on a slow or</b> unresponsive network share.<b> Counting a folder's items now runs on its own</b> track, so a hung share can't hold up previews of your other files.</li>
<li><b>A document preview no longer goes blank after entering and leaving full</b> screen.<b> The Quick Look preview now reloads itself correctly when the window</b> returns from full screen.</li>
<li><b>Files you can't open now explain why again in the preview pane.</b> For documents shown via Quick Look, a "you don't have permission" or "file not found" note is shown when the file can't be read — matching the rest of the app.</li>
<li><b>The folder "N items" line now matches the list.</b> When Show Hidden Files is on, the preview pane's item count includes hidden items too, so it agrees with what you see.</li>
<li><b>App bundles show their size in the preview pane</b> once measured, matching the Size column and status bar.</li>
<li><b>Files with many Finder tags show a "+N" indicator</b> instead of silently cutting the extra tags off.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
